.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "MyUtils" "MyUtils Library"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines containing a search string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep
function searches the file for lines containing
.B search_str .
Matching lines are stored in dynamically allocated memory and returned through
.B matches .
The caller is responsible for freeing the allocated memory.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines on success.
Returns -1 if an invalid argument is provided or a file error or memory allocation error occurs.
